+## Flip-rate (the "world affects poker choices" acceptance metric)
+
+`scripts/flip-rate.mjs` (run: `npx vite-node scripts/flip-rate.mjs`) is the permanent counterfactual metric: at every play it picks the argmax selection with specializations ON, re-picks on a clone with EVERY region's specialization nulled, and records whether the chosen selection changed. It measures BOTH conditions over the SAME disjoint eval-* seed set (eval-0..29, 12 plays each = 360 plays per condition — the documented ≥30-seed ≥300-play bar). This is not a human win-rate; it measures how often the regional layer decides a selection.
+
+| Condition | BEFORE (flat additive) | AFTER (non-match penalty) |
+|---|---|---|
+| (a) as-shipped (Pair awake) | 14/360 = **3.9%** (19/480 = 4.0% on the coordinator's independent 40-seed/480-play measurement) | 25/360 = **6.9%** |
+| (b) all three awake | 5/360 = **1.4%** (4/480 = 0.8% independent) | 7/360 = **1.9%** |
+
